-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Here's an update to the current 1993 listing of articles that reference
the Internet.  The list is in chronological order and includes both magazines
and newspaper articles.  This is a list of general interest not technical
articles.  Each reference has the following format:
 
  Article name
  Publication, Author, Date
  Summary
 
Some references don't have a summary because I've either not read them myself
or those who forwarded the reference to me did not provide one.  Thanks to
all those who contributed.  Keep those cards and letters coming!
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Commercialization of the Internet: Catching the Ear of Ten Million Users"
Online Access, Michael Strangelove, June 1993
 
"Get the Amateurs Out of High Tech,"
Upside, T. J. Rogers, June 1993
 
"Building the On Ramp to the Electronic Highway (A $2.5 billion deal may launch
an era of cooperation between phone and cable firms),"
Time, v 141 n 22, May 31, 1993, p 52-53, Philip Elmer-Dewitt, (reported by
John F. Dickerson and Thomas McCarroll/New York)
 
[Focuses on entertainment implications of the electronic superhighway
and the cableco-telco partnerships springing up around the US]
 
